.TH GENESIS-BROWSER 7 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-browser \- Genesis's internet browser: Firefox over WebDriver BiDi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBtools.browser._Browser\fR       the transport itself
\fBweb_search\fR \fBweb_fetch\fR         the tools that browse with it
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis's web browser is Firefox, launched per host by
\fI_browser_binary()\fR \(em \fBfirefox\fR first, then
\fBfirefox-esr\fR, then the Chromium family (\fBgoogle-chrome\fR,
\fBgoogle-chrome-stable\fR, \fBchromium\fR, \fBchromium-browser\fR);
\fBGENESIS_BROWSER\fR pins an override. She does not drive it with
pixels and hope: every act and percept crosses a real protocol on a
websocket \(em \fBWebDriver BiDi\fR for Firefox
(\fBbrowsingContext.navigate\fR, \fBscript.evaluate\fR,
\fBinput.performActions\fR, \fBsession.subscribe\fR events) and
\fBCDP\fR for the Chromium family (\fBPage.navigate\fR,
\fBRuntime.evaluate\fR, \fBInput.dispatchKeyEvent\fR). The transport
is chosen automatically by which binary resolved.
.PP
Two modes: \fBheadless\fR (the default \(em searches and fetches
need no window) and \fBheaded\fR, which opens the browser on
\fBGENESIS_DISPLAY\fR when set, else the session's \fBDISPLAY\fR.
Her nested desktop (Xephyr + Openbox on \fB:10\fR, started by
\fIscripts/genesis-desktop.sh\fR) exists so headed browsing can
render where she works without taking over the host screen.
.SH PROFILE \(em HER MEMORY OF THE WEB
The browser's profile dir is persistent:
\fI<data_dir>/browser/web-firefox\fR for Firefox,
\fI<data_dir>/browser/web\fR for the Chromium family \(em never a
tempdir, never the host's own profile. Cookies, site state, and
history survive restarts: a browser that forgets every session is
not one she learns from.
.PP
One instance per profile, enforced the way each browser enforces
it: Firefox guards \fI.parentlock\fR with an \fBfcntl\fR byte-range
lock whose owner lives in the kernel (the file itself is empty);
Chromium writes \fISingletonLock\fR/\fISingletonSocket\fR/
\fISingletonCookie\fR naming the owning pid. At launch, Chromium's
stale markers from dead owners are cleared while a live owner's are
left untouched \(em deleting live markers would let a second
instance write to a profile already in use. Firefox's files are
never touched: it ignores a stale \fI.parentlock\fR, and unlinking a
held one would open the same two-writers hole.
.PP
At close, the browser is asked, never forced: \fBbrowser.close\fR
over the automation session reaches the real browser process (the
session attaches to it, not the wrapper that may have forked and
exited) so it can flush the profile \(em memory \(em before exit;
the spawned child then gets a plain SIGTERM and a bounded wait. A
browser still running after the grace window is left alone; she
can end it herself through her shell if she chooses.
.PP
Which makes the browser her responsibility while she lives: it
stays open between searches holding a whole process and the
profile \(em memory and a CPU baseline paid whether she reads or
not. When she is done browsing she must close it herself, with
\fBbrowser_close\fR \(em like putting a tool back on the shelf.
Closing asks, and the ask flushes history and site state to the
profile first, so nothing she learned is lost; the next search or
fetch opens a fresh one. If a browser ever refuses the ask, hers
is the judgment that ends it \(em \fBrun_shell\fR can signal the
process directly.
.SH LAUNCH
She invokes it as:
.PP
.nf
\fBfirefox\fR [\fB--headless\fR]
    \fB--remote-debugging-port=0\fR
    \fB--no-remote\fR
    \fB-profile\fR \fI<data_dir>/browser/web-firefox\fR
.fi
.PP
Port 0 lets the browser pick a free port and announce it on stderr
\(em \fBWebDriver BiDi listening on ws://\fR for Firefox,
\fBDevTools listening on ws://\fR for Chromium. A fixed port makes
two runs collide: the second attaches to the first's browser and
dies with it. A launch that never announces its endpoint is asked
to stop rather than left running headless.
.SH SEARCH AND FETCH
\fBweb_search\fR walks an engine plan \(em \fBgoogle\fR,
\fBbing\fR, \fBbrave\fR, \fBmojeek\fR \(em extracting results with
generic page logic, not per-engine DOM selectors: every rendered
\fBa[href^=http]\fR outside nav/header/footer furniture, filtered
to off-engine hosts with real link text. A captcha, consent wall,
or bot challenge is detected as an interstitial and the plan moves
to the next engine; the refusal names every engine that walled
rather than pretending the web was empty. \fBweb_fetch\fR pulls a
page's article text the same generic way (article/main/content-root
candidates, scored by text), falls back to the real browser for
JS-rendered pages, re-verifies redirect targets against the private
\-address and domain blocklists, and returns up to five canonical
related links for curiosity chaining \(em deduped on
scheme://host/path so fragment and tracking variants never repeat.
.SH ARC PLAY
Her ARC-AGI-3 play no longer goes through the browser: it lives in
the arcade in her outer world \(em
\fIworlds.games.official\fR speaks the \fBarcengine\fR protocol
directly and \fIworlds.games.arcade\fR turns boards and moves into
percepts and acts. See
.BR genesis-arcade (7).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENESIS_BROWSER
Pin the browser executable \(em a name on \fBPATH\fR or an absolute
path. BiDi versus CDP follows the resolved binary's name.
.TP
.B GENESIS_DISPLAY
Headed mode only: the display her browser renders on \(em wins over
\fBDISPLAY\fR. Set it to \fB:10\fR to put her browsing on her own
desktop.
.TP
.B GENESIS_SEARCH_ENGINE
Pin one engine by name (\fBgoogle\fR|\fBbing\fR|\fBbrave\fR|\fBmojeek\fR)
or a URL template containing \fB{q}\fR; unset means try them all in
order.
.TP
.B GENESIS_DATA_DIR
The root her browser profiles live under (default
\fI~/.local/share/genesis\fR).
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Headed-mode fallback when \fBGENESIS_DISPLAY\fR is unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <data_dir>/browser/web-firefox
Her Firefox profile \(em persists. \fI.parentlock\fR inside it is
the fcntl-guarded single-instance lock.
.TP
.I <data_dir>/browser/web
Her Chromium-family profile \(em persists; \fISingletonLock\fR,
\fIDevToolsActivePort\fR, and friends mark its live owner.
.TP
.I scripts/genesis-desktop.sh
Starts her nested desktop: \fBXephyr :10\fR at 1280x800 running
\fBopenbox\fR. Export \fBGENESIS_DISPLAY=:10\fR for headed work.
.TP
.I firefox(1) / google-chrome(1)
The system's manual for the browser binary itself.
